  "measures": [],
  "notes": "A stretched pulse from a Ti:sapphire amplifier front end (100 fs sech² at its transform limit, leaving with +20 000 fs² of chirp) is compressed by a Treacy grating pair: two parallel 600 l/mm gratings, 30° incidence, first order, 61.24 mm apart, chosen so their −20 000 fs² cancels the chirp (Treacy 1969). Open the Pulse tab on each screen: before, a pulse over half a picosecond long; after, back near 100 fs. The colours leave the pair side by side (spatial chirp): a real compressor sends them back through with a roof mirror to put them together again. Move Grating 2 along the beam, or sweep its x, to see the duration pass through its minimum."
